WEBVTT

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.230
Tada!

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.410
No way.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.050
What about this?

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.210
Or this one?

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.520
Or this?

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.220
I don't know which to choose.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.830
This could work.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:58.000
Why do I have to look after them?

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.640
I guess I'll take my body
board just in case.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.340
A class trip, huh?

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.950
Most of the students who chose the C trip are
members of the chorus and art clubs...

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.750
so I would hoping you would chaperone
them, Kamikura-sensei.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.280
Chaperone them? You want me to do it?

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:20.890
Thank you.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.760
Give me a break.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.710
I've got my hands full with just Elis.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.080
Onii-chan.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:33.060
What do you think of this bikini?

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.570
Whatever you do, put on some clothes!

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.540
Do you think this would be better?

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.040
You can't wear either of those!

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.070
Can't you wear something bigger?

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:45.360
You know, one of those black ones that
cover you from top to bottom.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.550
Students should wear their
school swimsuits!

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.690
I wish I had a cuter swimsuit.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:00.990
How many years has it been since
I last went to the beach?

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:08.270
I guess this will do.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.490
Yeah, right.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.840
I see. I didn't know you had
a school swimsuit fetish.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.380
I don't! That's not what
I'm trying to say...

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.650
I can't decide, so I'll bring
all my swimsuits.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.910
Hey, wear a one piece! A one piece suit!

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.750
Got that, Elis?

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.680
I'm not wearing an old lady swimsuit.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.360
Well, I guess they are for old ladies.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:46.040
Emerald Green Temptation

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:42.950
All right!

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.970
We'll go to the beach!
And the hot springs!

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.810
And maybe there will
be fireworks at night.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:54.300
Onii-chan's been pretty tired lately,
so I'll have to give him a massage.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.420
I'll experience the joys of the
sea and the mountains...

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.450
and walk along the beach
with Onii-cahn.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.270
Two nights and three days
might not be enough.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:05.150
Do whatever you want.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:10.500
I wish we could have gone to Okinawa
or Hawaii or Polynesia.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.230
This'll be fun.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.610
There's a lot to see.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.720
Shota, what's that black circle?

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.100
It's a secret.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.610
Who is that?

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.710
That's Hashizume Shota-kun.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.440
Can't you remember your
own classmates?

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:27.780
Hooray!

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.480
We're finally going.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:36.820
They say this class trip is meant
to expand our cultural horizons.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:39.260
But the real focus of this trip...

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:43.400
Is the amazing night the three
of us will give you!

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:47.510
The juniors are full of energy.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.770
I want to go home.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:53.750
I will meet you there tomorrow night.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:58.710
Students, please be careful
and enjoy yourselves.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.480
Chaperones, look after our students.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.690
Let's start with the A trip!

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.020
What is this?

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:12.900
A test of courage on the second night?

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.600
Apparently, it's an annual custom.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.150
A custom?

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:26.820
Nadesico Academy

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.280
Every year, the sophomores and juniors
welcome the freshmen...

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:28.770
by wracking their brains for
ways to frighten them.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.370
Why would they do something like that?

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.910
It's ritual meant to establish the
dignity of the upperclassmen...

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.360
in an age of a disappearing hierarchy.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:38.780
But the bus assignments were chosen at random
without regard for class standing.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:43.060
Simply put, it's just some
tasteless hazing.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.310
We've been put in charge
of the test of courage.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.390
What are we supposed to do?

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:51.630
Top Secret

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:56.280
Sort the costumes the sophomore
and juniors brought...

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:00.740
set up the course, keep an eye on
the students. That kind of thing.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.040
Hiroki, weren't you listening
at the preliminary meeting?

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:09.710
The superintendent told me just
two days ago I'd be chaperoning.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.880
Why do we have to manage
the test of courage?

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.850
Sorry, but you're on your own.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:18.630
What? You can't do that.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:20.340
The two of us have been
assigned to do it...

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.250
and there's no way I can
do it on my own.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:23.960
I said I don't want to!

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:26.030
In that case, what do we
need teachers for?

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:29.080
They sure are close.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.170
Huh?

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:33.300
Hashizume-kun, sorry.
I can't see the front.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.740
Oh, sorry.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.820
I wonder what they're arguing about.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.330
Who cares?

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.550
I sense a storm coming...

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.880
Would to try the local specialty...

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.090
chocolate matcha wasabi crackers?

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.760
I'll give it a try.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.450
Thanks for the food.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:00.600
Interesting.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.000
Give me one.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.000
I'll try one, too.

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:12.010
Huh? Elis-chan?

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:15.420
I'm a teacher. Why do I have
to run a test of courage?

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.430
This is stupid.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:19.080
I'll do anything for my job.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.580
That's right, it's your job. You do it.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.990
Are you sure you just don't like ghosts?

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:25.870
That's...

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.830
That's not...

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.430
Onii-chan...

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:43.010
Leave your bags where they are
and line up by the rope way.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.060
Sorry, I didn't mean to scare you.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:51.370
I think you'd be fighting with Onii-chan.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:56.320
It must be tough living with an unreasonable
person like Hiroki.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:01.150
And I'm sorry you have to work at the same
school as that stubborn old man.

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.500
I know.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.600
You go on ahead.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.330
Hiroki's out of control.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.800
Leave your luggage on the bus!

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:11.610
Hurry up and form two lines!

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:12.820
Don't stop moving!

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:15.240
Sensei, what's at the top?

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:16.920
A famous art museum.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:18.840
Sounds boring.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:20.690
In addition to exhibits...

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:25.730
they've got hands on glass blowing
and ceramics making corners.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:26.470
Onii-chan...

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:31.120
Don't forget your report or painting
is due when we get back.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.480
Lame.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.240
Now, now. Let's go.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:37.890
Sensei, I'm afraid of heights.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:38.910
That's a problem.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.550
This rope way is the
only way to the top.

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:42.750
Onii-chan...

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:44.410
But I really can't do it!

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.760
All right. It's a little our of the
way, but we'll get a taxi.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:50.480
Close your eyes and sing a
song and you'll be fine!

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:52.600
Stop fussing around and hurry up.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.320
You can do it!

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:56.550
Okay.

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:58.580
You can do it, Sumire-san!

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:02.100
What?

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.630
That was harsh.

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:07.540
Learning to travel with a group is
another one of this trip's goals.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.990
We can't go easy on them.

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.150
Is that so?

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:21.270
Sorry.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:23.060
What were you doing?

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.570
That's a secret.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.610
Shota, over here.

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:27.510
A secret?

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:34.220
This is amazing.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:40.900
The bubble flew.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:45.180
The bubble flew up to the roof.

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:44.060
What's wrong, Sumire-san?

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:47.460
Apparently, she'll fall off the rope
way if she stops singing.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:50.320
The bubble flew up to the roof, and...

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:49.400
Can't she sing anything better?

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:54.970
It popped and disappeared.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:56.780
Misaki-senpai?

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:57.930
Misaki?

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:59.280
Sumire-san?

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.180
Sensei!

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:02.750
What's wrong?

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:05.280
Are you okay, Misaki?

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:09.420
The wind is blowing.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:12.590
Let's blow some bubbles.

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.640
Are you okay?

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:36.130
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:39.970
Who knew her bubble
lifeline would burst?

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:42.320
She picked the wrong song.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.500
Can you drink this?

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:49.290
Yes, thank you.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.770
Kiri, this is because of
your weird suggestion.

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:54.280
Misaki-san, I'm really sorry.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.300
Don't be. I'm sorry for
causing you trouble.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:00.170
Referring to Kikyo-sensei
without an honorific?

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:01.670
That's suspicious.

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:07.010
I'm still a little dizzy, but I'll be fine.

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:09.240
Rest here until you feel better.

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:10.950
I'll stay with her.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:12.180
Okay.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.990
Hey, Fujinami.

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:24.080
There's no food or drink allowed
inside the museum.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.330
Go spit out your gum.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:27.280
Okay.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:31.640
Hey.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.400
Can I go with you?

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:36.330
Uh, sure.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:37.890
Let's start over here.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:49.550
I've been looking forward to
coming here for a whlie.

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:54.290
Hosen-san, do you like ceramics, too?

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:56.820
Huh? What?

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:00.460
You can try your hand
at pottery over there.

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:02.830
I just remembered I have
something to do.

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:04.130
Sorry. Thanks, though.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:05.470
What? Oh...

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:14.580
Thank you.

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:17.890
Seems like Misaki Sumire
is doing okay now.

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:19.680
I just saw her over there.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.770
I'm too rough for this.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.390
I lack delicacy.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.720
You finally noticed?

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:30.530
I must not be cut out to be a teacher.

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:34.330
And you were just lecturing
me about this.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:36.540
Maybe.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.990
The students will be returning
in an hour.

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:48.360
There's no time to be feeling
down, Kikyo-sensei.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:48.980
Huh?

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:51.800
I'll check the costumes...

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.860
so why don't you help me plan the
route for the test of courage?

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:55.990
All right.

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:58.720
I was thinking about it earlier...

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.930
and I thought we could start with something
right after they pass through the torii...

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:05.700
Hosen-san.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:08.000
We're on our way to see the paintings.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.220
Would you like to come with us?

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.470
Sure.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.260
Look at those two.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:17.980
They're in charge this year?

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:21.570
What are you talking about?

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:24.050
You'll find out tomorrow.

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:28.350
What? You're scaring me.

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:36.260
We're here.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.830
Your attention, everyone.

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:44.580
You're free to do whatever
you want until dinner.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:47.860
You can go to the beach,
head to the hotsprings...

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:50.840
go for a walk, take a nap,
or do anything else.

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.280
All right!

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:55.920
After dinner, the sophomores and
juniors will bring their bags...

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:59.120
and meet in the “Wasabi Room.”

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.780
Are we having a planning meeting?

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:04.610
Join us, sophomores.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.440
We should go with something
covered in blood...

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.410
Good idea, horror queen!

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:09.860
I think we should do something
traditional...

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.490
It's almost time.

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:15.730
Yes.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:17.620
Time for what?

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.430
Planning the test of courage.

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:22.570
Are the third years really running
a test of courage?

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.410
They're serious about it.

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:26.840
It's a vicious circle in which they take revenge
for their own first year experience...

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.350
by scaring the new freshmen.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:32.390
If you can make it through this year,
it'll be your turn next time.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:34.030
Take care.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:35.690
Unbelievable.

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:37.270
See you later.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:39.240
You're not going to the beach?

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.390
Not interested.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.520
Shota really is weird.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.630
Onii-chan.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.900
We're about to go to the beach.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:51.160
Do you want to come with us?

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:53.530
I'm not your Onii-chan here.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.780
You're such a pain.

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:59.610
I've got a lot to do, so why
don't you go by yourselves?

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.320
Be back in time for dinner.

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:03.050
You're no fun.

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:06.420
Elis-chan, hurry up!

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:07.550
Okay.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:08.590
Hey...

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:14.560
Uh, you're wearing a one
piece swimsuit, right?

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.240
What's that got to do with you?

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.700
Don't blame me if someone attacks you!

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:27.200
I can't believe her.

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:47.060
Ready, set, go!

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:13.780
Tomoko-chan, you came.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:18.920
I don't think I've been in the
ocean since I was a kid.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:20.880
Really?

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:24.190
Once, before I was even old
enough to remember.

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:27.240
Aren't you glad you came?

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:29.770
Yes, the cold water feels kind of nice.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:41.650
Elis-chan, where are you going?

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:45.000
I'm feeling cold, so I'm heading back.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:53.990
They'll start at the torii, pass behind the
shrine, and go once around the yard.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:58.300
We can place students here
and there along the course.

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:00.130
Sounds good to me.

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:04.330
It gets dark at night, so let's keep the course
short and finish this up quickly.

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.270
Are you really that scared?

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:08.000
I'm not scared.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.210
I just don't want anyone to get hurt.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:14.140
You don't have to impress me.

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:19.580
Okay.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:22.950
Kiri, you're scared of ghosts, aren't you?

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:26.260
No I'm not. I just hate being frightened.

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:27.950
Oh, I remember!

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:32.100
Didn't you pass out during our
middle school festival...

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:35.330
when you saw yourself dressed
as a ghost in a mirror?

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:39.400
That was a long time ago!

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:42.240
Over there!

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:57.250
Oh, no.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:06.440
Sorry.

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:16.390
Shrine Shortcut

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.330
Onii-chan?

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:34.510
The wind feels nice.

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:37.630
Yeah, it does.

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.140
No! Help me, Onii-chan!

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:51.460
Hosen-san? It's me, Hashizume Shota!

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.750
Hashizume-kun?

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:57.500
Sorry for scaring you. Are you all right?

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:05.830
You got your clothes dirty.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.900
And you're covered in mud.

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:09.270
What's in there?

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:13.230
Pottery clay. I got it at
the bottom of the cliff.

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:15.400
Clay?

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:19.150
I've been interested in ceramics
since I was little.

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:22.190
I make pottery with clay
from all over the place.

00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:24.070
Hosen-san, where are you going?

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:25.350
Onii-chan...

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:26.440
I need to go.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:31.080
It's almost time for dinner, Hosen-san!

00:19:32.630 --> 00:19:36.040
Do you remember the festival
we went to in high school?

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.020
What festival?

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:41.110
We made fun of the night market
and paid homage to the shrine.

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:45.400
Didn't we buy a bear mask?

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:48.570
It was Cho Hakkai from the Saiyuki.

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:51.300
That's right, that was it!

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:57.010
We laughed until our stomachs hurt and drank
Ramune on the stone shrine steps.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.680
That's right. I remember that.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:06.820
But we didn't have enough money,
so we had to share one.

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:07.950
That's right.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:13.890
Onii-chan, I've never seen you
laugh like that before.

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:18.770
I feel so nostalgic.

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:23.020
Like it was so long ago, but also
just happened yesterday.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:24.870
You're right.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:30.170
Today's just like that evening.

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:31.790
Yeah.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:41.750
Did you say something?

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:44.420
No. Maybe we should head back soon.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:46.500
Okay.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:04.580
No... No way!

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:08.650
Hosen-san, what's wrong?

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:27.630
No... No... No...

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:12.140
Hey, Onii-chan...

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:17.290
why do men think girls screaming
in fear are cute?

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:21.610
That's because we feel like
we want to protect them.

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:28.020
But it's got to be a cute
scream, doesn't it?

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:30.310
Those aren't screams. They're shouts.

00:23:30.310 --> 00:23:31.250
Hiyah!

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:34.060
Wait, why am I protecting you?

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:36.550
Next episode, “Sand Beige Sea Roar.”

00:23:36.550 --> 00:23:38.910
Love happens after dark!
